# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values.

# Convex self-hosted backend secret — generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
CONVEX_INSTANCE_SECRET=

# Shared secret proving a caller is Convex when it reaches recipe-service.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32. MUST match the value set on the Convex
# deployment via `convex env set RECIPE_SERVICE_SECRET ...`.
RECIPE_SERVICE_SECRET=

# Optional: USDA FoodData Central key for nutrition estimation (BL-0036). Free
# from https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-key-signup.html; rate limited to 1,000
# requests/hour. Leave it unset and nutrition still works — it falls back to the
# checked-in snapshot of common ingredients and reports honestly on the rest, so
# a missing key costs coverage, never correctness. FDC data is CC0, so lookups
# are cached permanently and steady-state traffic approaches zero.
# FDC_API_KEY=

# Real store prices (BL-0046) — OFF by default, and off is the shipped state.
# Setting PRICING_STORE_PROVIDER to "kroger" turns on the store chooser and lets
# a user who picks a store see that store's shelf prices; leaving it unset leaves
# every list priced from the checked-in BLS averages, which is what every user
# sees today. Credentials are required too — either one missing leaves the
# feature disabled rather than failing, so a half-configured deployment still
# prices every list.
#
# Get credentials by registering at https://developer.kroger.com (free; OAuth2
# client credentials, ~10,000 Products calls/day). Registering is also where the
# developer terms (https://developer-ce.kroger.com/terms) are accepted — read
# them before enabling this. Their caching clause is what bounds our cache:
# prices are held in memory only and expire per the response's own cache header.
# See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-17-real-store-prices-design.md.
#
# NEVER commit real values. This file is the example; .env is gitignored.
# PRICING_STORE_PROVIDER=kroger
# KROGER_CLIENT_ID=
# KROGER_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Observability (BL-0027). Set this and run `docker compose --profile obs up`
# to send traces to the local Grafana stack. Leave unset for a quiet stack.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://alloy:4318

# The Convex deployment reads OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT from its own env, not
# this file. To emit Convex action spans, set it on the deployment:
#   convex env set OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT http://alloy:4318
# Leave unset for a quiet backend (spans are a no-op without it).
